{"name":"Cambridge Blue","hex":"#a3c1ad","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cambridge Blue (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cambridge Blue is the shade of green commonly used by sports teams from the University of Cambridge. There is contextual and historical variation. The colour used since the mid-20th century by Cambridge University Boat Club is greener than that used by Cambridge University R.U.F.C.. This rowing colour was created when Alf Twinn, the boatman from 1934 to 1984, added more yellow to this shade, reportedly to distinguish it from the rugby club's colour."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1d/Cambridge_blue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cambridge_Blue_(colour)"},{"title":"Blue (university sport)","blocks":[{"text":"A blue is an award of sporting colours earned by athletes at some universities and schools for competition at the highest level. The awarding of blues began at Oxford and Cambridge universities in England. They are now awarded at a number of other British universities and at some universities in Australia and New Zealand."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_(university_sport)"},{"title":"Cambridge","blocks":[{"text":"Cambridge is a city and non-metropolitan district in the county of Cambridgeshire, England. It is the county town of Cambridgeshire and is located on the River Cam, 55 miles (89 km) north of London. As of the 2021 United Kingdom census, the population of the City of Cambridge was 145,700; the population of the wider built-up area was 181,137. There is archaeological evidence of settlement in the area dating back to as early as the Bronze Age, and Cambridge became an important trading centre during the Roman and Viking eras. The first town charters were granted in the 12th century, although modern city status was not officially conferred until 1951."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Cambridge_-_Kings_College_vue_des_backs.jpg/330px-Cambridge_-_Kings_College_vue_des_backs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cambridge"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Cambridge-half-blue-blazer.jpg/500px-Cambridge-half-blue-blazer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Cambridge-half-blue-blazer.jpg/500px-Cambridge-half-blue-blazer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cambridge University Rifle Association half blue blazer and bow tie","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACambridge-half-blue-blazer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Oxford-half-blue-blazer.jpg/330px-Oxford-half-blue-blazer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Oxford-half-blue-blazer.jpg/330px-Oxford-half-blue-blazer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Oxford University Rifle Club half blue blazer and tie","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOxford-half-blue-blazer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Punts%2C_River_Cam_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5936313.jpg/500px-Punts%2C_River_Cam_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5936313.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Punts%2C_River_Cam_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5936313.jpg/500px-Punts%2C_River_Cam_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5936313.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APunts%2C_River_Cam_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5936313.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Church_of_St_Mary_the_Great_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5897670.jpg/500px-Church_of_St_Mary_the_Great_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5897670.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Church_of_St_Mary_the_Great_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5897670.jpg/500px-Church_of_St_Mary_the_Great_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5897670.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChurch_of_St_Mary_the_Great_-_geograph.org.uk_-_5897670.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikime